NiceMon V9.9
? lists the commands
> ?
r [ADDR]      run the program at ADDR, or at 00008000; r 0 restarts
l             enter lines of ADDR WORD in hex, as a .bin file has them
load NAME     load the .bin file NAME of the SD card, as l loads lines
save NAME A N save N words from A, both in hex, as the .bin file NAME
del NAME      delete the file NAME of the SD card
tftp IP NAME  load the .bin file NAME from the TFTP server at IP
tftp IP [PAT] list the files of tools/tftpd.py at IP, or those of PAT
d [ADDR] [N]  show N words from ADDR, in hex, or the next ones
u [ADDR] [N]  disassemble N instructions from ADDR, or the next ones
dir [SLOT]    list the files of the SD card in SLOT, or of the card mounted
i [A.B.C.D]   show the IP address, or set it, such as 192.168.1.65
i dhcp        get the IP address from a DHCP server
m [MAC]       show the MAC address, or set it, such as 02:4E:49:43:45:01
baud [RATE]   show the UART baud rate, or set it, such as 921600
time [D T]    show the local time, or set it, such as 2026-11-11 14:30:00
time ntp [S Z] set it from the time server S, Z local time less UTC, +01:00
c             clear the screen
v             the version
h             halt the core
?             the commands
CRSR up down  scroll back a row, before a command
PgUp PgDn     a page; on the MEGA65 CTRL and MEGA with CRSR up or down
